{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And your name shall be Avraham.</b> This letter Heh that was added to him is the last letter of the Name, and with it he had the power of generation descending from him. And so we find in Avraham that he is called a throne (משרה), and it is the completion of the building, for so it is above — the completion of the supernal Chariot (המרכבה העליונה)." "<b>For a father of a multitude of nations have I made you.</b> Our father Avraham, peace be upon him, was the father of the world, like the first man, who was the father of a multitude of nations from whom all generations descend. And so we find that Avraham is called 'man' (אדם), from what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded on (Joshua 14:15): ״האדם הגדול בענקים״ — 'the great man among the giants' — this is Avraham. And I have already alluded to this in the section of Bereshit." "<b>And in this parashah</b> the commandment of circumcision was given to him, and thirteen covenants were sealed upon it, and they are alluded to there."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "He writes דרשו רז\"ל followed by a citation of Joshua 14:15, apparently citing the scriptural verse that the Sages expounded rather than attributing the verse itself to them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:52.143000797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}